```cpp
void release() {
    if (ref_count.fetch_sub(1) == 1) {
        // BUG: Non-atomic gap between count hitting zero and freeing.
        // A concurrent thread with an existence guarantee could increment
        // the counter from 0 to 1 and assume the object is valid!
        delete this; 
    }
}
```

fix:
Use an atomic RMW loop that fails to increment if the reference count is already zero.
```cpp
bool try_acquire() {
    int count = ref_count.load();
    while (count > 0) {
        if (ref_count.compare_exchange_weak(count, count + 1)) {
            return true;
        }
    }
    return false; // Already dead, cannot re-acquire
}
```
